      "text": "1. Set the equation based on the problem statement: $x^2 + 1 = y^3$ and $x^2 - 1 = z^2$.\n2. Rewrite the equations: $x^2 = y^3 - 1$, $x^2 = z^2 + 1$.\n3. Use the method of differences: $(x^2 + 1) - (x^2 - 1) = y^3 + 1 - z^2 - 1$.\n4. Apply the difference of cubes formula: $x^2 = (y + z)(y^2 - yz + z^2) + 2$.\n5. There are two cases to consider: (1) $y^2 - yz + z^2 = 2$; (2) $y^2 - yz + z^2 = -2$. The first case is not reasonable because the discriminant $y^2 + 4z^2$ is not divisible by $3$.\n6. Utilize the difference of squares formula: $x^2 = (y + z)(y + z - 1) + 1$.\n7. Apply the positive integer constraint: $y + z \\geq 2$.\n8. Summarize the result of the problem: Jane is 15 years old.\n\nThus, Jane is $\\boxed{15}$ years old.",
